itions. RAIRO-Inform. Theor. 18(4): 387–394.\n\n(Open in a new window)Google Scholar\n\n  * Mousavi, H. (2016). Automatic theorem proving in Walnut. Available at: arXiv.org/1603.06017.\n\n(Open in a new window)Google Scholar\n\n  * OEIS Foundation Inc. (2025). The On-Line Encyclopedia of Integer Sequences. Published electronically at oeis.org.\n\n(Open in a new window)Google Scholar\n\n  * Shallit, J. (2022). The logical approach to automatic sequences: exploring combinatorics on words with Walnut. Cambridge: Cambridge University Press.\n\n(Open in a new window)Google Scholar\n\n  * Shallit, J. (2024). Proving properties of some greedily-defined integer recurrences via automata theory. Theor. Comput. Sci. 988: 114363.\n\n(Open in a new window)Web of Science ®(Open in a new window)Google Scholar\n\n  * Uspensky, J. (1927). On a problem arising out of the theory of a certain game. Amer. Math. Monthly 34: 516–521.\n\n(Open in a new window)Google Scholar--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n[2502.00799] Minimal matroids in dependency posets: algorithms and applications to computing irreducible decompositions of circuit varieties (https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2502.00799)\nciteturn6search5 [wordlim: 200] Published: 1.8 years ago; Crawled: 2 months ago; View a PDF of the paper titled Minimal matroids in dependency posets: algorithms and applications to computing irreducible decompositions of circuit varieties, by Emiliano Liwski and Fatemeh Mohammadi ... View a PDF of the paper titled Minimal matroids in dependency posets: algorithms and applications to computing irreducible decompositions of circuit varieties, by Emiliano Liwski and Fatemeh Mohammadi\n\n# Mathematics > Combinatorics\n\n[Submitted on 2 Feb 2025]\n\n# Title:Minimal matroids in dependency posets: algorithms and applications to computing irreducible decompositions of circuit varieties\n\nAuthors:Emiliano Liwski, Fatemeh Mohammadi\n\nView a PDF of the paper titled Minimal matroids in dependency posets: algorithms and applications to computing irreducible decompositions of circuit varieties, by Emiliano Liwski and Fatemeh Mohammadi\n\nView PDF HTML (experimental)\n\n> Abstract:We study point-line configurations, their minimal matroids, and their associated circuit varieties. We present an algorithm for identifying the minimal matroids of these configurations with respect to dependency order, or equivalently, the maximal matroids with respect to weak order, and use it to determine the irreducible decomposition of their corresponding circuit varieties. Our algorithm is applied to several classical configurations, including the Fano matroid, affine plane of order three, MacLane, and Pappus configurations. Additionally, we explore the connection to a conjecture by Jackson and Tanigawa, which provides a criterion for the uniqueness of the minimal matroids.\nSubjects:  | Combinatorics (math.CO); Commutative Algebra (math.AC); Algebraic Geometry (math.AG)\nCite as:  | arXiv:2502.00799 [math.CO]\n   | (or arXiv:2502.00799v1 [math.CO] for this version)\n   | https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2502.00799 arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\n\n## Submission history\n\nFrom: Emiliano Liwski [view email]\n[v1] Sun, 2 Feb 2025 13:39:45 UTC (480 KB)\n\nFull-text links:\n\n## Access Paper:\n\nView a PDF of the paper titled Minimal matroids in dependency posets: algorithms and applications to computing irreducible decompositions of circuit varieties, by Emiliano Liwski and Fatemeh Mohammadi\n\n  * View PDF\n  * HTML (experimental)\n  * TeX Source\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBeyond adjacency: Graph encoding with reachability and shortest paths (https://arxiv.org/abs/2509.20247)\nciteturn6academia14 [wordlim: 200] Published: 1.1 years ago; Title: Beyond adjacency: Graph encoding with reachability and shortest paths\nAuthors: Shiqiang Zhang, Ruth Misener\nTitle: Beyond adjacency: Graph encoding with reachability and shortest paths\nAuthors: Shiqiang Zhang, Ruth Misener\nDate: Wed Sep 24 15:35:12 2025\n\nGraph-structured data is central to many scientific and industrial domains, where the goal is often to optimize objectives defined over graph structures. Given the combinatorial complexity of graph spaces, such optimization problems are typically addressed using heuristic methods, and it remains unclear how to systematically incorporate structural constraints to effectively reduce the search space. This paper introduces explicit optimization formulations for graph search space that encode properties such as reachability and shortest paths. We provide theoretical guarantees demonstrating the correctness and completeness of our graph encoding. To address the symmetry issues arising from graph isomorphism, we propose lexicographic constraints over neighborhoods to eliminate symmetries and theoretically prove that adding those constraints will not reduce the original graph space. Our graph encoding, along with the corresponding symmetry-breaking constraints, forms the basis for downstream optimization tasks over graph spaces.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMinimal matroids in dependency posets: algorithms and applications to computing irreducible decompositions of circuit varieties (https://arxiv.org/abs/2502.00799)\nciteturn6academia15 [wordlim: 200] Published: 1.8 years ago; Title: Minimal matroids in dependency posets: algorithms and applications to computing irreducible decompositions of circuit varieties\nTitle: Minimal matroids in dependency posets: algorithms and applications to computing irreducible decompositions of circuit varieties\nAuthors: Emiliano Liwski, Fatemeh Mohammadi\nDate: Sun Feb  2 13:39:45 2025\n\nWe study point-line configurations, their minimal matroids, and their associated circuit varieties. We present an algorithm for identifying the minimal matroids of these configurations with respect to dependency order, or equivalently, the maximal matroids with respect to weak order, and use it to determine the irreducible decomposition of their corresponding circuit varieties. Our algorithm is applied to several classical configurations, including the Fano matroid, affine plane of order three, MacLane, and Pappus configurations. Additionally, we explore the connection to a conjecture by Jackson and Tanigawa, which provides a criterion for the uniqueness of the minimal matroids.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nANTONIO VERA LOPEZ - Universidad del País Vasco / Euskal Herriko Unibertsitatea (https://ekoizpen-zientifikoa.ehu.eus/investigadores/126836/publicaciones?lang=en)\nciteturn6search6 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 4 weeks ago; Fibonacci-like partitions and their associated piecewise-defined permutations ... Israel Journal of Mathematics, Vol. ... Journal of Group Theory, Vol.\n\nImage: Foto de ANTONIO\n\n# ANTONIO\nVERA LOPEZ\n\n## PROFESORADO CATEDRATICO/A DE UNIVERSIDAD\n\nDétail Publications Collaboration Thèses Projets\n\n[Input] Accès ouvert\n\n## Publications (71) Publications de ANTONIO VERA LOPEZ\n\n### 2026\n\n  1. Fibonacci-like partitions and their associated piecewise-defined permutations\n\nFibonacci Quarterly\n\n### 2017\n\n  1. Combinatorics related to Higman's conjecture I: Parallelogramic digraphs and dispositions\n\nLinear Algebra and Its Applications, Vol. 530, pp. 414-444\n\n  2. On higman’s conjecture\n\nElectronic Journal of Linear Algebra, Vol. 32, pp. 151-162\n\n### 2016\n\n  1. Equalities on the number of conjugacy classes of the Sylow p-subgroups of GL(n, q)\n\nIsrael Journal of Mathematics, Vol. 214, Núm. 2, pp. 675-697\n\n### 2015\n\n  1. Counting conjugacy classes for unitriangular matrices\n\nLinear Algebra and Its Applications, Vol. 486, pp. 275-294\n\n### 2014\n\n  1. A generalization of Catalan numbers\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------