X\n\nCopy\n\n@misc{hegedüs2025newupperboundssize, title={New upper bounds for the size of set systems with restricted intersections modulo prime powers}, author={Gábor Hegedüs}, year={2025}, eprint={2501.02925}, archivePrefix={arXiv}, primaryClass={math.CO}, url={https://arxiv.org/abs/2501.02925}, }--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nA101642 - OEIS (https://oeis.org/A101642)\nciteturn6search11 [wordlim: 200] Published: 21.8 years ago; Crawled: 1.6 years ago; Jon Asier Bárcena-Petisco, Luis Martínez, María Merino, Juan Manuel Montoya, and Antonio Vera-López, Fibonacci-like partitions and their associated piecewise-defined permutations, arXiv:2503.19696 [math.CO], 2025.\nSmeets】, Mar 20 2024\n\nThe asymptotic density of this sequence is 1/phi^4 = A094214^4 = 0.145898... . - Amiram Eldar, Mar 24 2025\n\nLINKS\n\nA.H.M. Smeets, Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..20000\n\nJon Asier Bárcena-Petisco, Luis Martínez, María Merino, Juan Manuel Montoya, and Antonio Vera-López, Fibonacci-like partitions and their associated piecewise-defined permutations, arXiv:2503.19696 [math.CO], 2025. See p. 5.\n\nW. F. Lunnon, Proof of formula, 2008.\n\nFORMULA\n\nFrom Michel Dekking, Dec 23 2019: (Start)\n\na(n) = 3*A000201(n+1) + 2n - 3.\n\na(n) = A101345(n) + A000201(n+1) + n + 1. (End)\n\nMATHEMATICA\n\nzeck[n_Integer] := Block[{k = Ceiling[ Log[ GoldenRatio, n*Sqrt[5]]], t = n, fr = {}}, While[k > 1, If[t >= Fibonacci[k], AppendTo[ fr, 1]; t = t - Fibonacci[k], AppendTo[fr, 0]]; k-- ]; FromDigits[fr]]; kfp[n_, m_] := Block[{y = Reverse[ IntegerDigits[ zeck[ n]]], z = Reverse[ IntegerDigits[ zeck[ m]]]}, Sum[ y[[i]]*z[[j]]*Fibonacci[i + j + 2], {i, Length[z1]}, {j, Length[z2]}]]; (* Robert G. Wilson v, Feb 04 2005 *)\n\nTable[ kfp[3, n], {n, 50}] (* Robert G. Wilson v, Feb 04 2005 *)\n\nArray[3*Floor[(# + 1)*GoldenRatio] + 2*# - 3 &, 100] (* Paolo Xausa, Mar 23 2024 *)\n\nPROG\n\n(Python)\n\nfrom math import isqrt\n\ndef A101642(n): return 3*(n+1+isqrt(5*(n+1)**2)>>1)+(n<<1)-3 # Chai Wah Wu, Aug 29 2022\n\nCROSSREFS\n\nThird row of array in A101330.\n\nCf. A101345 = Knuth's Fibonacci (or circle) product \"2 o n\".\n\nCf. A000201, A003849, A094214.\n\nKEYWORD\n\nnonn\n\nAUTHOR\n\nN. J. A. Sloane, Jan 26 2005\n\nEXTENSIONS\n\nMore terms from David Applegate, Jan 26 2005\n\nMore terms from Robert G. Wilson v, Feb 04 2005\n\nSTATUS\n\napproved--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nOWR-2025-9 (https://ems.press/content/serial-article-files/51353)\nciteturn6search16 [wordlim: 200] Published: 1.3 years ago; Optimization, Theoretical Computer Science and Algebraic Geometry 411 ... MacLane configuration \\(M\\) and its minimal matroids ... Mohammadi, *Minimal matroids in dependency posets: algorithms and applications to computing irreducible decompositions of circuit varieties*, arXiv preprint arXiv:2502.00799 (2025).\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMathematisches Forschungsinstitut Oberwolfach (https://oa.tib.eu/renate/server/api/core/bitstreams/1b45f1ba-d23c-42ea-ab74-566973ccf925/content)\nciteturn6search17 [wordlim: 200] Published: 6 months ago; Optimization, Theoretical Computer Science and Algebraic Geometry ... MacLane conﬁguration M and its minimal matroids ... Mohammadi, Minimal matroids in dependency posets: algorithms and\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nA polynomial method over formal power series (https://arxiv.cnoctave.top/pdf/2610.39460)\nciteturn6search18 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 4 days ago; Štefankovič, Set systems with restricted intersections modulo prime powers, J. ... Raigorodskii, Asymptotic study of the maximum number of edges in a uniform hypergraph with one forbidden intersection, Sb. ... Raigorodskii, New upper bounds for the independence numbers of graphs with vertices in \\(\\{-1,0,1\\}^n\\) and their applications to problems of the chro